3. What is the goal of selfish mining?
a) to reduce the transaction fees paid by users
b)
c) let honest miners waste computational power
d) to earn a larger share of the block rewards than the pool's share of the hash power
correct: c) d)
explanation: Bitcoin adjusts mining 
difficulty so that blocks arrive every ~10 minutes. Orphaned honest blocks slow down
the main chain, so difficulty eventually drops, and then the selfish pool earns more per unit
of time too.

